  "prefLabel": "En 1011.02 System Impact Study Agreement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1011.02 System Impact Study Agreement. Separate from and in addition to the application fee pursuant to En 1004.01, all expected costs necessary for the utility to conduct necessary EDS study shall be set forth in a separate SISA between the utility and the applicant, issued by the utility, the payment of which shall be due in full prior to the commencement of work. The utility shall make their best faith efforts to estimate the actual costs necessary to study the EDS for interconnection of the applicant’s proposed facility. As set forth in the SISA, the applicant shall bear and be responsible for all costs to interconnect the facility to the system, including, without limitation, all necessary system modification costs. Should any dollars remain from the SISA, they shall be included in the true up as a part of the final accounting described in En 1018.11.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
